From c021f18099a812a08f88aa13ef7034dcdd4a5e75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mick <sirmick@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Apr 2026 19:35:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Unicorn PPC: fix qemu_ram_block_from_host for host=NULL
 prealloc blocks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

REAL_ADDRESSING guests (mac-phoenix PPC) legitimately mmap RAM at host
virtual address 0 via MAP_FIXED, so a RAMBlock with host == NULL is a
valid prealloc mapping — not an unmapped block. The reverse-lookup code
used block->host truthiness (MRU fast-path) and block->host == NULL (loop)
as "not mapped" sentinels, so it skipped mac-phoenix's RAM block and
returned NULL. That bubbled up as RAM_ADDR_INVALID in
qemu_ram_addr_from_host_nofail → abort(), killing Unicorn as soon as
TCG tried to translate code at a low RAM address (first hit: guest PC
0x00037410 during a transition-vector bctrl).

Distinguish by the RAM_PREALLOC flag: if it's set, the caller explicitly
supplied the host pointer and NULL is intentional; only skip blocks that
are both unmapped (host == NULL) and not prealloc. uc_mem_map_ptr already
tolerated NULL; this is the matching change on the reverse path.

Unicorn PPC boundary trace now advances from ~114 EmulOps (SIGABRT) to
555, matching KPX's 557-op reference under MACEMU_PPC_NO_IRQ.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 qemu/exec.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/qemu/exec.c b/qemu/exec.c
index 38eaa748..2b9014f1 100644
--- a/qemu/exec.c
+++ b/qemu/exec.c
@@ -1257,14 +1257,21 @@ RAMBlock *qemu_ram_block_from_host(struct uc_struct *uc, void *ptr,
     RAMBlock *block;
     uint8_t *host = ptr;
 
+    /* REAL_ADDRESSING guests (e.g. mac-phoenix PPC) may legitimately map RAM
+     * at host virtual address 0 via mmap MAP_FIXED, so block->host == NULL is
+     * a valid base for prealloc'ed blocks. Don't use block->host truthiness
+     * as a proxy for "mapped". */
     block = uc->ram_list.mru_block;
-    if (block && block->host && host - block->host < block->max_length) {
+    if (block && (block->host || (block->flags & RAM_PREALLOC)) &&
+        host - block->host < block->max_length) {
         goto found;
     }
 
     RAMBLOCK_FOREACH(block) {
-        /* This case append when the block is not mapped. */
-        if (block->host == NULL) {
+        /* Skip blocks that are truly not mapped. A prealloc block whose host
+         * pointer is NULL was explicitly mapped at host address 0 by the
+         * caller; keep it. */
+        if (block->host == NULL && !(block->flags & RAM_PREALLOC)) {
             continue;
         }
         if (host - block->host < block->max_length) {
